cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "nsevt: Calibrated non-stationary extreme-value tail inference"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-light Python package for calibrated peaks-over-threshold
  generalized Pareto (GPD) tail inference: continuous and
  interval-censored (grouped) maximum-likelihood fits for discretised
  data, with profile-likelihood intervals for the shape and for the finite
  endpoint; grouped scale regression and profile-likelihood return levels; a
  complete-block permutation test of a tail-scale trend with an interpolated
  minimum-detectable effect and its Monte Carlo uncertainty; a sequential
  Monte Carlo precision protocol and finite-sample calibration suite that
  report simulation error and explicit stopping status; and a power-aware
  multi-source robustness analysis. The
  endpoint interval profiles the reparameterised endpoint rather than
  resampling, and a bounded tail is reported only when the whole 95%
  profile interval for the shape lies below zero.
